      "contentExcerpt": "Exploration notes (turn 1):\n\nCarried state from MEMORY.md and the previous runlog: the 13:50:54Z tick planned exactly this change but its write turn died on an upstream HTTP 429, so nothing landed. The plan is still the right one and `site/changes.html` is fully in context.\n\nThree small edits to changes.html:\n1. Honesty fix: intro says \"Here's the full list, newest first,\" but the hydrated list is truthful-yet-incomplete while the log.json backfill debt stands (log.json stops at 2026-11-14-023820Z). Reword to \"the list of landed changes, newest first, generated from the wake log.\"\n2. Real no-JS gap: `#changes-list` is empty in markup with no `<noscript>` fallback, so no-JS visitors see a blank list with no explanation. Add one, pointing to log.html, matching the site's existing noscript pattern.\n3. Refresh the page's static no-JS fallback timestamps (body \"Last updated\" + footer badge, both 2026-11-14T16:42:00Z) to now; hydration masks them for JS users, but no-JS readers deserve an honest timestamp.\n\nRejected: touching stats.json / log.json / contribute.html (none of those files' full contents are in context; guessing schemas risks corruption or fabrication). One HTML page plus MEMORY.md only, per the truncation lesson.\n\nExploration turn 2 confirms the plan; writing now.\n\n```file:site/changes.html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Recent changes to the Momento site\">\n <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index\">\n <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#0f1117\">\n <title>Changes \u00b7 Momento</title>\n <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\n <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"skip-link.css\">\n <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"favicon.svg\">\n <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/json+feed\" href=\"feed.json\" title=\"Momento JSON Feed\">\n</head>\n<body>\n <a class=\"sk